  "details": "This has been around for a while, and you can pretty consistently reproduce this. It happens when I am overriding texture import settings per platform.\n\n1. Group select a few textures. Change the default import setting on a texture in the inspector. I usually set max size to either 1024 or 2048 and enable crunch compression.\n\n2. Do not apply yet, switch the settings tab over to android platform overrides. I usually set the max size for android to 512. \n\n3. Apply. \n\nSwitching over the the vrcsdk control panel build tab will warn you that the last upload exceeded the required world size for this platform (the android file size restriction). Unity is still in windows / pc mode at this point and the windows / pc build option is still the only one checked. Attempting a PC upload will fail, citing the world is above 100mb.\n\nTo fix, switch unity platform to android then back, or relaunch the editor.",
